  "note": "Triennial election of the seven electoral divisions of Moira rural district, one member each, polled on 5 June 1952. There were no contests: seven nominations were received for the seven seats. J. C. G. McQuoid was the only new member, for Donacloney in place of W. H. Irwin. Returned unopposed."
